        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12539992/comment/13194623",
          "id": "13194623",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=rcmuir",
            "name": "rcmuir",
            "key": "rcmuir",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150"
            },
            "displayName": "Robert Muir",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "{quote}\nI'm thinking a possibility could be to expose possible decompounds as part of Kuromoji's Token interface.\n{quote}\n\nI like this idea: I think it would give the most flexibility, we would populate some attribute from \nToken just like we do today for other attributes, and then actual indexing of compounds can be \ncontrolled with a configurable tokenfilter.\n\nLong term, this lets the tokenizer stay a tokenizer and prevents it from growing too complex.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=rcmuir",
            "name": "rcmuir",
            "key": "rcmuir",
            "avatarUrls": {
